From 0f8126506cd13809520df6d993f3ac59a09a04b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VDN-H3 Authors <vdn-h3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 10:18:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Group offloading: send module buffers back with streams

With use_stream=True a ModuleGroup onloads every group module's parameters AND buffers,
and keeps a CPU copy of both in cpu_param_dict -- but _offload_to_memory pointed only the
parameters back at their CPU copies. Every buffer inside an offloaded group stayed on the
accelerator, so block-level offload with streams gathered all of a model's buffers there.
The non-stream path, module.to(offload_device), moves them with the parameters.

VDN-H3's fp8 Linears keep their weights in buffers. Block-offloading the fp8 transformer
with streams on a 24 GB card piled those weights up until it ran out of memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/diffusers/hooks/group_offloading.py | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/diffusers/hooks/group_offloading.py b/src/diffusers/hooks/group_offloading.py
index 10d3f0c..28e73a6 100644
--- a/src/diffusers/hooks/group_offloading.py
+++ b/src/diffusers/hooks/group_offloading.py
@@ -322,6 +322,11 @@ class ModuleGroup:
                         _restore_torchao_tensor(param, self.cpu_param_dict[param])
                     else:
                         param.data = self.cpu_param_dict[param]
+                for buffer in group_module.buffers():
+                    if _is_torchao_tensor(buffer):
+                        _restore_torchao_tensor(buffer, self.cpu_param_dict[buffer])
+                    else:
+                        buffer.data = self.cpu_param_dict[buffer]
             for param in self.parameters:
                 if _is_torchao_tensor(param):
                     _restore_torchao_tensor(param, self.cpu_param_dict[param])
